course: dictionary
lesson: 9583
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear different coats. Streak can mean a line, a run of wins, a part of someone's character, or to move very fast. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «That is how they catch fool's gold, pyrite, which glitters like gold but is harder, much lighter and leaves a black streak.» Here a streak is a mark left behind, because you can leave a mark but not a winning run.
explain: Look at the clues. «It rushes into the air so fast that it heats up and burns, leaving a bright streak.» Something that rushes fast and leaves a bright mark across the sky is making a streak of light. The clues tell you the meaning.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Blueberry pancakes with too much baking soda get green streaks.» If you swap in mark, the sentence still makes sense: green marks, not green wins. Swapping the meaning in is a quick check you can always use.
fact: A streak can be a long, thin line or mark of a different colour, like a streak of paint.
fact: A streak can also be a run of the same result many times in a row, like a winning streak.
fact: A streak in someone's character is a small part of it, like a mean streak or a stubborn streak.
fact: To streak means to move very fast, or to mark something with streaks.
fact: Geologists identify minerals by hardness, colour, lustre (shine), streak and how they break, so the streak of a rock is a useful clue.
exercise: «A streak of paint ran down the wall.» What is a streak here? | *A long, thin mark of a different colour | A kind of shoe | A rainy day | A loud noise
exercise: «The team had a winning streak all season.» What does streak mean? | A long thin line on a shirt | A sad feeling | *A run of wins, one after another | A type of fast train
exercise: «Her stubborn streak showed when she refused to stop.» What is a streak in someone's character? | A kind of game | A large chest of drawers | *A small part of their character | A type of hat
test: «The comet streaks across the sky.» What does streaks mean here? | *Moves very fast across | Paints the sky with pictures | Stays still for hours | Falls slowly to the ground
test: Geologists use the streak of a rock to tell minerals apart. What does streak mean here? | *The colour of its powder | Where it was dug up | How loudly it rings | Its weight on the scale
exam: Which sentence uses streak to mean a run of the same result? | *«The team won seven games in a row, their longest streak yet.» | «The sun streaked through the window.» | «The lightning left a bright streak.» | «He has a mean streak.»
